UID:123752-1791628200-1791639000@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Roots of Discovery: Sands of Knowledge
DESCRIPTION:Journey through the rich cultures of the Muslim world and discover an extraordinary legacy of curiosity\, creativity and innovation. Explore how scholars\, artists and thinkers preserved ancient knowledge\, transformed it through new discoveries\, and shared ideas that would influence Europe and help shape our modern understanding of mathematics\, astronomy\, medicine\, art\, architecture and the natural world. \nPresentations\n\n12:30 – 1pm\, SECU Daily Planet Theater\nHearts\, Minds\, and Healing: How Caring for Others Connects Us All\nCaring for others is rarely a one-way exchange; what we extend to others returns to shape us. This session transitions between the heart and the mind. It brings the compassion and service at the center of Islamic tradition into conversation with empathy and self-awareness\, the cornerstones of emotional intelligence\, and asks how each becomes a form of healing. What emerges is a picture of what encourages individuals make a meaning of their own stories\, allows them to feel seen and heard. Recognition\, in turn\, is what binds a community together \nAbout the speaker\nFatma Wasel was born in Kuwait\, raised in Yemen\, and has Egyptian roots. She holds a Doctorate in Executive Leadership focused on emotional intelligence and cross-cultural integration. A U.S. State Department alumna\, educator\, trainer\, activist\, and linguist\, she has worked across government\, nonprofit\, and private sectors nationally and internationally. \n\n1 – 1:30pm\, SECU Daily Planet Theater\nHealing and Discovery: The Muslim Legacy in Medicine and Engineering\nFrom Al-Zahrawi\, the father of modern surgery whose surgical texts shaped European medicine for centuries\, to Al-Jazari’s ingenious mechanical inventions\, this talk explores the golden age of Muslim scientific achievement in medicine and engineering. Discover how scholars across the Islamic world advanced surgery\, pharmacology\, and mechanical design in ways that continue to influence science today. \nAbout the speaker\nMohsen Zakaib is a physician-in-training with a multidisciplinary background in nuclear engineering\, business\, and Islamic studies. He holds bachelor’s and master’s degrees in Nuclear Engineering\, an MBA\, and a bachelor’s in Islamic Studies. Mohsen serves as Director of Development at the Lighthouse Project and co-founded RISE at the Islamic Association of Raleigh. \nActivities\nNature Research Center Lobby\nCreatures beyond the Sand: Wildlife Across a Continent \nNC Museum of Natural Sciences\nJourney beyond the desert and discover the incredible diversity of animals found across Africa and its surrounding islands. Meet fascinating creatures and explore the unique adaptations that help them thrive in habitats from forests and wetlands to grasslands and beyond. \nMapping the Heavens: Stars\, Time & Discovery\nArtist Ummah\nLook to the skies and discover how Muslim scholars mapped the stars\, measured time and expanded our understanding of the universe. \nHealing Through Knowledge: The Roots of Medicine\nArtist Ummah\nDiscover how Muslim physicians studied the human body\, advanced medical treatments and preserved knowledge that helped shape modern medicine. \nThe Living Lineage: A Journey into the Muslim Arts \nArtist Ummah\nJourney through timeless traditions of calligraphy\, geometry\, tezhip\, ebru\, and other contemporary art forms inspired by the classical Muslim arts. Discover how artists across North Carolina are reimagining these rich traditions while honoring their heritage and helping keep these beautiful art forms alive for generations to come. \nInteractive Arabic Calligraphy Demonstration \nArtist Ummah\nExperience a live Arabic calligraphy demonstration with local artist\, who will showcase the art of Arabic lettering and write visitors´names in Arabic. \nSips of History: Coffee\, Tea & Tradition  \nArtist Ummah\nExplore the fascinating journey of coffee from its roots in the Muslim world\, where it was cultivated\, brewed\, and celebrated as part of social and intellectual life.  \nA Cup of Connection \nSalt & Cheeni \nEnjoy a complimentary sample of freshly brewed coffee with Salt & Cheeni! Discover how the right grind and brewing method bring out the best in every bean\, and explore how coffee is more than just a drink—it’s conversation\, connection\, and comfort in a cup. \n\nAbout our Collaborator \nArtist Ummah is a community-driven art organization that uplifts diverse Muslim voices and builds bridges of understanding between communities. To learn more about what they do\, visit: Artist Ummah \n\nRoots of Discovery series offers a meaningful platform where communities can share their stories in their own voice — through hands-on science\, artistic expression and cultural traditions — while showcasing the connections between culture\, nature and scientific discovery. \nNext in the series:  \n\nNov 10 — Roots of Discovery: Festival of Light
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/roots-of-discovery-sands-of-knowledge/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,General Events,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Teens
