UID:123122-1791883800-1791894600@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:STEAM Career Showcase for Students with Disabilities
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 13th annual STEAM Career Showcase for Students with Disabilities – a free event for learners in grades 6–12. Connect with role models with disabilities who have thriving careers in the fields of Science\, Technology\, Engineering\, Arts\, and Math (STEAM). Learn about their personal journeys and strategies for success. Gain practical knowledge that you can apply to your interests and future career paths. \nASL interpretation and live captions will be provided for welcome\, keynote presentation\, and panel discussion. Registration closes on Friday\, October 9th. \nRegister Now \n  \n\nSchedule\n9:30am: Doors Open & Check In \n10:00am: Welcome \n10:15am: Keynote Presentation with Q&A \n11:00am – 12:30 pm: Opportunity Fair with Exhibitors \nNoon – 12:30pm: Panel Discussion \n\nKeynote Speaker\n \nDr. Louis Vaught\nPostdoctoral Research Associate in Chemical and Mechanical Engineering at The University of Tulsa \nAn engineer who develops new materials and manufacturing technologies\, Dr. Vaught has worked on some exciting projects. These include wearable batteries woven into clothing\, plastics that survive harsh environments like the North Pole\, and even reusable glue for building satellites in orbit.\n\n–\nPanelists\n \nTrusha Patel\nPhysical Therapy Student at Campbell University \n\nTrusha aims to help people get back to the things they love doing after an injury\, illness or life-changing event. As an amputee and future physical therapist\, her personal experience inspired her passion for rehabilitation and helping others.\n\n\n–\n\n\nLacey Roy\nNeurosociology Student at UNC Chapel Hill \n\n\n\nStruggling in school before being diagnosed with Audiological Processing Disorder and gaining the right accessibility tools\, Lacey now thrives in her studies. Her research\, with Dr. Natasha Parikh\, examines how culture affects whether a dream or goal is considered possible.\n\n\n\n–\nExhibitors\n\nNCMNS Teen Programs\nFind out about programs & volunteer opportunities for middle and high school students\, right here at the Museum.\n–\nCatalyst at NC State\nGet information about the free\, award-winning program that prepares high school students with disabilities for careers in STEM fields.\n–\nAutism Society of North Carolina\nSpeak with an employment specialist from ASNC who helps autistic job seekers in their search.\n–\nYouth LEAD NC\nLearn about the NC Youth Leadership Forum on NC State’s campus\, where participants get an on-site college experience before even graduating from high school.\n–\nNC ABLE Program\nGain knowledge about financial resources for people with disabilities\, including savings accounts and investments.\n–\n\n\n\nVirtual Option\nFor those unable to join in person\, the welcome and keynote speeches will be livestreamed on the Museum’s YouTube channel.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/steam-career-showcase-2026/
LOCATION:Nature Exploration Center\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Accessible,K-12 Students,Youth Science Program
ORGANIZER;CN="Samantha%20Frigerio":MAILTO:Samantha.Frigerio@naturalsciences.org
