SUMMARY:Fall is for Planting: A Native Plant Garden Tour
DESCRIPTION:Join staff from the Library of North Carolina’s Government and Heritage Library and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences for a Native Plant Walk focusing on why fall is the ideal time for planting. \nThis plant walk will explore native plantings in the NC Department of Natural and Cultural Resources’ Native Plant Meadow and the NC Museum of Natural Science’s Native Plant Garden. The event will take place primarily outdoors\, with participants traveling approximately a half-mile round-trip via paved sidewalks. \nPlease join us and learn why fall is the ideal time for planting natives in North Carolina. \nRegister Here \n 
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/fall-is-for-planting-a-native-plant-garden-tour/
LOCATION:Archives\, History\, & State Library Building\, 109 East Jones\, Raleigh\, North Carolina\, 27601
CATEGORIES:Adults,Outdoor Experiences,Special Events
